From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:25:50 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: gtactive3wifi: kernel: big-core options explicit in
 the fragment

gen-kernel-config.sh starts from build/bringup/.config, so options that
only a bring-up build happened to enable (the Exynos9810 PoU erratum, the
energy model) vanished when cand/1030's config was generated after another
bring-up build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/bigcores.config | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/bigcores.config b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/bigcores.config
index 51f3190..b1a8d6f 100644
--- a/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/bigcores.config
+++ b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/bigcores.config
@@ -4,3 +4,11 @@
 CONFIG_EXYNOS9810_CPUCL1=y
 # report how far a secondary core got when it fails to come online
 CONFIG_ARM64_DEBUG_SECONDARY_BOOT=y
+# Mongoose M3 I-cache coherency (Samsung cleans to PoC; selects
+# ARM64_WORKAROUND_CLEAN_CACHE) and the energy model for the big cluster's
+# OPPs. Explicit: gen-kernel-config.sh starts from the last bring-up build's
+# .config, so a default-y symbol is not enough (cand/1030 lost both once).
+CONFIG_SAMSUNG_ERRATUM_EXYNOS9810_POU=y
+CONFIG_ENERGY_MODEL=y
+CONFIG_SCHED_MC=y
+CONFIG_HOTPLUG_CPU=y
